# Task 7 fix round 3 (b10937e47c)
commit b10937e47cf367c7626f0f2326f896506018beeb
Author: Richard <richard@Richards-Mac-mini.local>
Date:   Mon Oct 19 10:33:28 2026 +0700

    fix(shellx): virtual PTY kill marks the child exited; demux hangs up when it stops
    
    A failed surface start dropped the startup guard (kill, then wait) before
    the master. With a snapshot filling the in-process pipe, the demux sat in
    the pipe write, so wait never returned and the resource-creation locks
    stayed held daemon-wide. kill now marks the child exited itself; the exit
    is still published only after the mirror's reader sees the pipe's end.
    
    The demux also shuts its socket down whenever its loop ends (E, protocol
    or read error, mirror gone), so the app sees EOF and unbinds at once
    instead of when the surface drops.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

